WEBVTT

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.020
Don't you desire freedom and rights, Hohenheim?

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.240
Do you plan to let your life end as a slave,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.360
without even obtaining your basic rights as a human?

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:20.450
If so, you might as well be living in this stuffy flask.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.270
The Other Side 
of the Gateway

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.270
The Other Side 
of the Gateway

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.930
Why?!

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.220
All right!

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.550
Finish him, Ed!

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.970
Why am I, someone who has obtained God,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.810
being defeated by the bare hands...

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:46.270
...of a mere human alchemist?

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.910
He did it!

00:00:58.910 --> 00:00:59.660
All right!

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.240
You showed him!

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:25.730
Man the fuck up!

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.230
Why are you getting swept away?!

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:28.650
M-My bad!

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.270
Stone...

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.570
Philosopher's stone!!

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:44.580
Give me your philosopher's stone!

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.830
Shit!

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:49.330
Greed!!

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.670
Idiot, you're going to get yourself dragged in!

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:52.500
Let go!

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.840
I refuse!

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.800
In order for me to become the Emperor, I need you!

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.090
That's just impossible!

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:02.050
I was born from Father to begin with.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:05.220
The force that's pulling me toward him is stronger than the one pulling me toward Lin Yao!

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.680
Nothing can be done!

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.480
Don't give up, Greed!

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.560
Keep trying!

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:12.690
Shit!

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.690
My body...!

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.570
God dammit!!

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.160
Well, it's a few ranks lower than being the king of the world,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.410
but I guess I wouldn't mind becoming the Emperor of Xing.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.790
We're gonna fight together, partner.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:33.790
That's the spirit!

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.670
What are you...

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.380
And this is goodbye.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.180
There's no need for you to be absorbed by him along with me.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.730
H-Hang on, Greed!

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:52.520
You just said that we were going to fight together!

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:55.320
This is foul play, dammit!

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.190
I thought you never told lies!

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.740
You can't let it end like this!

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.950
You totally fell for it though, shitty brat!

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.460
That was my first and final lie.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.960
Lan Fan has a philosopher's stone with her.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.670
Take it home with you, kid.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.210
Wait...

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:20.970
Wait!

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.470
Wait, Greed!!

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.430
Come, Lan Fan!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.640
Peace.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:34.060
Greed!

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.440
Greed!!

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.990
Curse you, Greed!!

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:47.450
I was able to free myself from an annoying brat.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:57.090
Why do you revolt against your father, Greed?!

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:00.380
Just going through a late puberty, pops.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.300
With this carbonization ability you gave me,

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.810
I'll turn us into the most brittle form of carbon, charcoal!

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.520
You little...!

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.810
Begone, fool!

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:20.980
Greed!!

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.320
Damn, I guess this is it...

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:39.040
Take a look in the damn mirror, brat.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.880
Friends are connected by the soul!

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.090
There's no way you'd forget!

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.470
Want to join us?

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.060
If you've got nowhere else to go, come with us.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:57.560
Man, both Lin and the midget totally made a fool out of me.

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:02.820
That was plenty...

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.780
Yeah, that was enough for me...

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.070
I don't need anything else...

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:17.830
Peace out, soul... brothers...

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:44.940
You guys...

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.450
My stones...

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.870
My philosopher's stones...

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:01.130
W-What?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:02.920
What is this?!

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.970
Go back to where you were born,

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.890
Dwarf in the Flask, Homunculus!

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:22.360
Why?!

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:25.860
I wanted to learn everything about this world!

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:32.410
I wanted to live freely in this vast world without being bound by anyone!

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.330
I...!

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.590
Why?!

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.260
Why won't you become mine?!

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:55.390
God, what are you unhappy with?!

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:58.140
Because you don't believe in yourself.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:06.020
You were born from humans after stealing other's power,

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.900
and yet, you were just clinging on to God the entire time.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:11.740
You haven't grown up at all.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:17.540
Did you think you'd be able to surpass humans if you let go of your seven desires?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.200
Don't make me laugh!

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.830
I wanted to become a perfect being!

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:25.250
I wanted to learn everything about this world!

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.500
What's wrong with wanting that?!

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.420
What's wrong with desiring it?!

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.180
What's wrong with wishing for it?!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.220
Who...

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:39.720
Who the hell are you?!

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.640
Who?!

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:44.770
Who the hell do you think you are?!

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:50.860
I'm the existence which you all refer to as "The World."

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:54.200
And "Universe," and "God,"

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:59.120
and "Truth," and "All," and "One."

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:03.160
And I am also yourself.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:08.630
Truth is what gives one the most fitting form of despair to insure them not to become conceited.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:14.630
He gives humans the most fitting form of despair to make sure humans don't become conceited.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.890
That is Truth.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:24.350
Thus, I'll also give you despair.

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:33.740
I don't want to go back!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.070
No!

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:40.740
Stop! I don't want to be bound there forever!

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:48.920
No! No!

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:50.840
No!!

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.130
Despair to the ones who become swelled with pride.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.630
What else should I have done?!

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:58.390
This is the end you desired.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.720
What should I have done?!

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.650
You probably foresaw the answer.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.870
What? What happened?

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.250
Did we win?

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:26.040
Yes.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:31.000
But... Alphonse has yet to come back from the other side.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.710
I'm... I'm so sorry...!

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.800
It's not your fault.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.180
It was Al's decision.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.350
Ed, we have a toll.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.770
Use it, it's a philosopher's stone.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.810
Use this to get Al back.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:50.770
I can't.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:57.950
We promised we'd never use a philosopher's stone to get our bodies back.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.040
There has to be another way.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.620
There HAS to be.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:10.920
Think...!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.380
Think!

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:13.960
Don't stop thinking!{dooon't stop believin'}

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.010
Edward.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:22.350
Use my life to bring Alphonse back.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.060
I've got just enough life left for one.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.270
Idiot!

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.980
There's no way I could do something like that!

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:35.320
It's our own fault that we lost our bodies!

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:40.320
I've said so many times that we won't use other's lives to get Al back!

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:43.410
Besides, why the hell do YOU have to give your life up?!

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.990
Because I'm your father.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:49.000
It's not about needs or reasoning.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.620
You two are precious to me.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:54.000
I want the both of you to live happily.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:11:00.510
I'm partially to blame for what happened to your bodies, since I left you to care for yourselves.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.180
I'm sorry.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:08.770
I've lived enough.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:13.020
Let me do something father-like for just this last time.

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:22.280
Don't be ridiculous, you good-for-nothing dad!{I know this sounds like shit, but 'dad' has to be in this line somehow; you'll see later on in the script. Make it sound better?}

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.570
Don't ever say something like that again!

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:26.530
I'll punch you!

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.340
I'm sorry, Edward...

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.270
Think...!

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.640
Think!

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:54.900
Aren't I supposed to be the youngest state alchemist of all time?!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:12:00.070
I can use alchemy without a transmutation circle because I saw Truth, right?!

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.070
There has to be a way!

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:03.400
There has to be!

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:15.080
I'm sure a lot of people are waiting for the day when you two get your bodies back.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:19.090
If there's a possibility, you should move forward.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:23.340
That's right. Don't give up.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:26.220
There... There has to be something.

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:27.970
Something!

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.570
Sir Al...

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.240
Sir Al...!

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.450
Sir Al!

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:55.160
May is crying so much for Al...

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:02.960
Zampano, Donkey Kong, and everyone from Briggs...

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:07.340
Major, Lin, Lan Fan...

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:10.850
Master, Dad...

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:21.320
May, step away for a sec.

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:50.760
That's...!

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:54.810
A human transmutation circle!

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.770
I'll be right back.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:03.480
The last transmutation that the Fullmetal Alchemist will ever do.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.120
Ed!

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.240
Ed!

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:15.490
Edward Elric!

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.140
So you came to get your brother back.

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:39.310
But how are you going to drag an entire human out?

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.850
What will you sacrifice?

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:43.150
Your entire body?

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:48.030
There's something huge right here that I can sacrifice.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:57.290
This is MY Gate of Truth.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.540
Which means I can do whatever I want with it.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:02.040
Am I wrong?

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:08.050
So that was your plan.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.800
But are you sure about that?

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:17.720
If you lose your Gate of Truth,
you'll never be able to use alchemy again.

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:20.060
Yeah...

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:25.610
You're right, all of alchemy is on the other side of this gate.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:29.320
But thanks to it, I was manipulated.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:35.780
I was shown the Truth, and believed that I could solve everything with alchemy.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.910
But I was wrong.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.330
I was just being arrogant.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:45.840
You're going to become an ordinary human who can't use alchemy?

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:50.380
I'm not going to "become" anything. I've always been an ordinary human.

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:56.010
I'm a puny human who couldn't even save a girl who was turned into a chimera.

00:15:56.550 --> 00:16:00.350
So you're sure you don't mind getting rid of that?

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:01.310
Ed!

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:02.060
Fullmetal!

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.020
Edward!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:03.560
Ed!

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:04.980
Edward Elric!

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:05.560
Ed!

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:06.440
Mr. Edward!

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.150
Ed!

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:08.770
Ed!

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.610
Even if I lose alchemy, I'll still have my friends.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.120
Correct, alchemist!

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.370
You've defeated me.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:23.000
Take everything you want!

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:29.000
The back door is over that way,

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:31.380
Edward Elric.

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.020
You were so reckless.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.270
Ditto.

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:58.410
Okay, let's go back. Together.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:16:59.280
Yeah.

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:17.680
Hey, he's awake!

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.550
You okay, Alphonse?

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:23.220
Mr. Zampano and Mr. Darius...

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:24.270
Everyone...

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:27.730
Dad!

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.730
Yo, welcome back.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:34.190
Yup.

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.570
Glad to be back.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:38.950
So warm...

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:41.450
Sir Al...

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:43.830
Sir Alphonse!

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:44.950
May!

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:47.960
I... I...!

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:52.130
That's right, I'm sorry.

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:53.960
I made you do something you didn't want to do.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:56.720
Thanks, May.

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:02.470
To those who are listening to Radio Capital:

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:07.480
Today, the squadrons led by Major General Armstrong and Colonel Mustang

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:10.190
captured Central Headquarters, assembly, and so on.

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:14.980
This was all in order to halt the actions of the upper echelon of the army;

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:20.240
they were planning a massive alchemy experiment that would sacrifice a great number of our citizens.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:26.870
Out of the masterminds who were planning on carrying out this evil experiment,

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:29.620
Brigadier General Clemin and Brigadier General Edison were captured,

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.630
and the soldiers who used to be under their command were disarmed.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:39.050
Führer President King Bradley and his son, Selim,

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:42.430
lost their lives in the midst of the confusion.

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:50.440
Colonel Mustang has voiced his intention to carry on the will of the Führer President and to keep our nation safe,

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:54.110
and that he'll consult with all whom it may concern about future measures.

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:04.160
You're the one who gave me blood, right?

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:09.870
Don't you desire freedom and rights, Hohenheim?

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:13.830
Then what does happiness mean to you?

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:17.840
Let's see... I won't ask for anything too extravagant,

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:22.130
but I guess I'd be happy if I could somehow leave this flask.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:30.350
You're right, Dwarf in the Flask, Homunculus.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:35.480
You were born from my blood.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:38.860
I...

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:44.910
Sir Hohenheim.

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:49.910
Both of your children have been safely hospitalized.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.250
Thank you. I appreciate it.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:56.500
No, I should be the one thanking you.

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:03.010
Edward Elric and Alphonse Elric.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:07.470
If it weren't for those two boys, this country would have fallen.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:10.020
Thank you very much.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:17.770
Thanks.

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:05.070
I'm home, Trisha.

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:13.580
Edward called me "Dad."

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:16.620
Though there was a "good-for-nothing" in front of it.

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:27.340
I always thought that it would be backbreaking to continue living longer than everyone else.

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:31.220
But by meeting you and our sons,

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:35.350
I was able to truly appreciate the fact that I was alive, from the bottom of my heart.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:38.480
It was a fulfilling life.

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:43.150
Yeah... it was more than enough.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:47.070
Thank you, Trisha.

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:53.120
But...

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:57.750
...somehow, I still want to live.

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:02.590
I really am a good-for-nothing.

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:12.100
Hohenheim!

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:15.720
What, you came home?

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:23.270
Idiot...

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:28.030
I've never seen a dead person look so happy.

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:34.870
The new morning we've finally found

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:34.870
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:39.250
is being hampered by the past.

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:39.250
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:44.710
What we chased after wasn't the future,

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:44.710
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

00:22:44.710 --> 00:22:48.550
but the past so full of remorse.

00:22:44.710 --> 00:22:48.550
Sugi bakari oikaketa

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:54.930
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:54.930
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

00:22:54.930 --> 00:22:59.100
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

00:22:54.930 --> 00:22:59.100
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:05.230
It's about now that a teardrop

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:05.230
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:09.900
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:09.900
Kattou ga koboreochiru

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:14.950
Will this rain ever stop?

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:14.950
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:20.040
I've been freezing for a long time.

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:20.040
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:25.130
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:25.130
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:30.130
I wonder if it could embrace me.

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:30.130
Tsutsumarete iikana

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:34.890
Today, the rain falls again;

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:34.890
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:40.100
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:40.100
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:45.190
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:45.190
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:53.910
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:53.910
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:06.040
The beginning is what comes after the ending.

00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:11.660
Carve out with your own hands a future, filled with hope.

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:16.930
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:21.080
Finale, Journey's End.

00:24:16.950 --> 00:24:21.080
Journey's End

00:24:21.080 --> 00:24:25.770
Take a step forward into the world called "life."
